        {
          "_comment": [
            "Eyelids. One quad per eye, sitting a hair proud of the face and",
            "hidden except for the few ticks of a blink.",
            "",
            "Each quad is UV-mapped to the BACK of the same head, one row down",
            "from the top, rather than to a colour or a new texture. The back of",
            "the head is the identical material with no eyes on it, so every skin",
            "- all eight materials, all sixteen professions, festive and worn -",
            "gets an eyelid in its own colour for free. Measured across all 408",
            "textures the front and back rows differ by a median of 23/255, which",
            "is straw grain, not a colour change.",
            "",
            "Only the two EDGE columns are covered, never the middle two, so the",
            "mouth on a worn face survives a blink. That also makes the pair",
            "symmetric about x, which means it does not matter which way round",
            "the box UV unwraps the front face - a fact the artwork gives no",
            "evidence for either way."
          ],
