        },
        {
          "_comment": [
            "Job badge, worn on the chest. Three flat quads stacked a hair proud",
            "of the torso, back to front: the rank-coloured frame and its dark",
            "backing plate, the job icon, and the corner flag for an immortal.",
            "",
            "They deliberately SHARE one UV rectangle (12x9 texels at 2,8 - free",
            "space in this sheet) and are told apart by texture, not by position.",
            "Each layer is a whole separate image selected at render time, so the",
            "cost of the system is 3 ranks + 17 jobs + 1 flag = 21 small files,",
            "instead of one texture per rank-job-flag combination, which would be",
            "over a thousand and would have to be regenerated for every new job.",
            "",
            "The quad is 4x3 model units carrying 12x9 texels, so the badge is at",
            "triple the density of the golem's own skin - a 4x3 patch of body",
            "texture could not hold a readable pickaxe."
          ],
